Pin MariaDB character_set_collations to pre-11.5.

MariaDB 11.5 changed which collation a bare CHARACTER SET resolves to,
so a table declaring only a character set no longer matches one
declaring neither. OpenStack migrations use both forms, so later
migration joining them fails with "Illegal mix of collations".

Pinning the mapping makes the two forms agree again, which fixes the
whole class rather than each migration that joins across it. Setting
collation-server does not help, because a table naming a character set
never consults the database default.

Prompt: Michael asked for the config fix and precheck we designed for
the MariaDB collation split to be generated as patches, on a new
worktree, so we can put them up for upstream review and see what
reviewers say. This change is the config half.

